# GitHub Pages runs Jekyll by default, which skips any path starting with an
# underscore and adds a build step this repo does not want. Nothing tracked here
# starts with "_" today - `git ls-files | findstr /R "^_"` is empty - so this file
# is insurance, not a fix: it makes Pages serve the folder verbatim, so a future
# _assets/ or _data/ directory cannot silently 404 in production only.
#
# The filename is the mechanism. Its contents are ignored.
